  "body": "Part of #894.\n\nA thread mill is not centre-cutting, and the thread-milling ride (`machining2d::thread_ride`) feeds it down the hole's axis before the first lead-in arc. That is air only if an earlier operation opened the hole. Nothing checks it: the `Thread` operation generates and verifies clean on a part whose hole is modelled, even when the program holds no drilling operation before it and the stock at the hole is solid. The gouge laws read the part (the hole is in the model), so they see nothing; the centre-cutting audit (`operation::plunge_solid`, `camcraft_motion::plunge_law`) is not asked for this kind, and it reads the raw stock, which would refuse every thread.\n\n**Effect:** forget the tap drill and the program plunges a thread mill into solid metal at plunge feed - a broken cutter, with no finding at generate, at verify or at the post gate.\n\n**Fix sketch:** read the stock the setup's earlier operations leave standing (the prior grid the drilling laws already read, `operation::drill_prior`) under each threaded hole: the tool's full cylinder down the axis and the first pass's lead-in must fall through air. Refuse by name at generate (\"the hole at (x, y) is not drilled yet - add a drilling operation before the thread\") and digest the program ahead in the stamp, so reordering the operations marks the thread Stale.\n\n**Done means:** a Thread operation with no drilled hole under it is refused by name; the same operation after a Drill of at least the tool's diameter generates; moving the Drill after the Thread turns it Stale and refuses; pinned by an app test. The milled `Bore` ride's axis entry gets the same reading or its own issue.\n",
